# Initial Setup's Accel Calibration page, ported from
# GCSViews/ConfigurationView/ConfigAccelerometerCalibration.cs.
#
# The claims: the page shows the .resx's words - the heading, the three sentences and the three
# buttons - with nothing in the prompt label; Calibrate Level sends MAV_CMD_PREFLIGHT_CALIBRATION
# with param5 2 and waits for the answer, and the vehicle's ACCEPTED turns the button's text to
# "Completed" (ConfigAccelerometerCalibration.cs:143-163); that text lives as long as the page
# object - leaving the page and coming back keeps it - and leaving the screen disposes the object,
# so the text is the Designer's again next time (Activate sets nothing but Calibrate Accel's
# Enabled, :27-31).
#
# This script presses Calibrate Level only, and here is why.
#
# * Calibrate Accel (param5 1) is the six-position conversation. SITL's airframe cannot be turned:
#   ArduPilot takes the level sample, then rejects the left one as too close to it and fails the
#   calibration ("Calibration FAILED"). A failed calibration zeroes the accelerometer offsets the
#   vehicle holds (AP_InertialSensor's _acal_event_failure), after which its pre-arm check says
#   "3D Accel calibration needed" until SITL restarts - and one left waiting for a position keeps
#   the vehicle calibrating, which refuses every other calibration. Either way every later script
#   that arms, or calibrates, would fail. The conversation - the start going out once, each
#   request and prompt written into the label, each click sending the position back, success or
#   failure ending it with "Done" disabled - is covered by the unit tests in
#   crates/mp-gui/src/config/accel_calibration.rs, against a scripted vehicle through the real
#   link.
# * Simple Accel Cal (param5 4) replaces INS_ACCOFFS_* and INS_ACCSCAL_* with what a still, level
#   SITL reads and saves them. tools/sitl/params/copter.parm sets the offsets to 0.001 "so INS is
#   recognised as being calibrated"; SITL's accelerometers read gravity with no bias, so the new
#   offsets would be zero or next to it, saved across restarts, and zero fails the same pre-arm
#   check. It too is covered by the unit tests.
# * Calibrate Level (param5 2) writes AHRS_TRIM_X and AHRS_TRIM_Y from what the level vehicle
#   reads - zero or next to it, which is what copter.parm leaves them - and recalibrates the gyros,
#   which ArduPilot does at every boot anyway. That is what this script leaves changed, and a
#   second run writes the same again: acceptable. The accelerometer offsets are checked unchanged
#   before and after.
#
# Needs SITL copter on tcp:127.0.0.1:5760 started from tools/sitl/params/copter.parm, disarmed and
# still (ArduPilot refuses a calibration while armed). Run as
#
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/config-accel.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

screen params
window 1600x1200
# A config.xml of its own, so the "Show me again?" boxes this script clicks are not already
# suppressed by the settings of the machine running it.
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
settle 6
# RawParamWarning, on the Full Parameter List's Activate (ConfigRawParams.cs:92): "Show me
# again?" unticked, so no later visit asks, and OK.
click raw-param-warning-again
click raw-param-warning-ok

# The page is listed once every parameter is in (isConnected && gotAllParams).
click param-download
settle 15
expect params.held > 1000
expect params.value.INS_ACCOFFS_X ~ 0.001
expect params.value.INS_ACCSCAL_X ~ 1.001

click tab-setup
settle 1
expect config.accel.active false
click setup-page-ConfigMandatory
click setup-page-ConfigAccelerometerCalibration
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigAccelerometerCalibration
expect setup.title Accel Calibration
expect config.accel.active true

# The page's words, and its controls as the Designer leaves them.
expect config.accel.heading Accelerometer Calibration
expect config.accel.text.accel ~ accelerometer Min/Max (3 axis).
expect config.accel.text.accel ~ This will ask you to place your autopilot on each edge.
expect config.accel.text.level ~ accelerometer offsets (1 axis/AHRS trims).
expect config.accel.text.simple ~ scale factors for level flight (1 axis).
expect config.accel.text.simple ~ This requires you to place your autopilot flat and level.
expect config.accel.calib Calibrate Accel
expect config.accel.calib.enabled true
expect config.accel.level Calibrate Level
expect config.accel.level.enabled true
expect config.accel.simple Simple Accel Cal
expect config.accel.simple.enabled true
expect config.accel.label none
expect config.accel.position 0
expect config.accel.incalibrate false
expect config.accel.subscribed false
expect config.accel.message none

# Calibrate Level: the command goes out, the vehicle levels and accepts, the text is Completed.
# The vehicle calibrates its gyros first and then samples the level, which takes seconds; the
# answer is waited for up to 25.
click accel-level
settle 10
expect config.accel.sent.level 1
expect config.accel.level Completed
expect config.accel.level.enabled true
expect config.accel.message none

# Nothing else was sent, and nothing else changed on the page or the vehicle's accelerometers.
expect config.accel.sent.start 0
expect config.accel.sent.position 0
expect config.accel.sent.simple 0
expect config.accel.calib Calibrate Accel
expect config.accel.calib.enabled true
expect config.accel.simple Simple Accel Cal
expect config.accel.label none
expect config.accel.subscribed false
expect params.value.INS_ACCOFFS_X ~ 0.001
expect params.value.INS_ACCSCAL_X ~ 1.001

# Another page and back: the page object is the same, and keeps its text.
click setup-page-ConfigFlightModes
expect setup.page ConfigFlightModes
expect config.accel.active false
click setup-page-ConfigAccelerometerCalibration
expect config.accel.active true
expect config.accel.level Completed

# Leaving the screen disposes the page object. Shown again - InitialSetup opens the page that was
# showing when it closed, its lastpagename - it is the Designer's.
click tab-params
settle 1
expect config.accel.active false
click tab-setup
settle 1
expect setup.page ConfigAccelerometerCalibration
expect config.accel.active true
expect config.accel.level Calibrate Level
expect config.accel.sent.level 1
